The likelihood of observing $n$ survival times $(T_1,\cdots,n_n)$ is given by the function

\begin{equation*}
L(\gamma_1,\cdots,\gamma_n|T_1,\cdots,n_n)=\prod_{i=1}^{n}
\left(\frac{1}{\gamma_i}\right) e^{-\sum_{j=1}^{n}
\gamma_j I(T_i<T_j)}\, \end{equation*}

with the constraint $\gamma_i\ge 0$ for all $i\in\{1,\cdots,n\}\in\mathcal{I}$
and the condition that at least one $\gamma_i$ is nonzero. 

The maximum likelihood estimator of the $\gamma_i$ under this model is given by
$\hat\gamma_i=\frac{1}{n}-\frac{1}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}I(T_i<T_j)}$ for all
$i\in\{1,\cdots,n\}\in\mathcal{I}$.

